What is RSA encryption?
RSA encryption is a technique used to send messages securely by encrypting the message by a key by the user then it sends it to the receiver the encrypted message then the user decrypts the message using specific key

What are Public Key and Private Key?
Public Key - It is used by a user to encrypt a message . It can be shared with anyone.
Private key - It is used to decrypt a message and it cannot be shared with anyone.
The message encrypted by a user's public key can only be decrypted by the same user's private key.

Why are two keys required instead of one?
One key is used to encrypt the message which is public key and other key is used to decrypt the message which is private key.
Suppose you want to send a message securely of someone , so you use their public key to encrypt the message and then send it to them,
then the user use its private key to decrypts the message and reads it .


What is the difference between symmetric and asymmetric encryption?
In symmetric encryption , the encryption and decryption key is same but
in asymmetric encryption , both keys are different which makes it more secure.

