What is a Digital Certificate?
A digital certificate is used to verify that the given public key actually belongs to this server , organisation.

What information does a certificate contain?
It contains
Certificate
│
├── Version
├── Serial Number
├── Signature Algorithm
├── Issuer
├── Valid From
├── Valid Until
├── Subject
├── Subject Public Key
├── Subject Alternative Name
├── Key Usage
├── Extended Key Usage
├── CA information
└── CA Digital Signature

What is a Certificate Authority (CA)?
It is the third party service that creates and signs the digital certificates.

Why can't anyone generate their own certificate for public trust?
This is because all computers come with some verified root ca which they trust but if user sign its own ca and certify it , they have to install their root ca on all the computers to trust it.

What is a Self-Signed Certificate?
A self-signed certificate is signed by the same entity that created it rather than by a publicly trusted CA.

What is SSL?
It is a security protocol used to securely establish a connection between two computers , eg browsers and server.

What is TLS?
TLS (Transport Layer Security) is a cryptographic protocol that provides secure communication over a network

Why is HTTPS secure?
Because HTTPS uses TLS protocol to establish secure connection between two computers.

Explain the SSL Handshake in your own words.
SSL handshake works like that.

Browser                            Server
   Hello------------------------>
       <------------------------- Hello
       <------------------------- Certificate
   Verify Certificate------------->
   <------Key Exchange------------>
   <------Secure Connection------->
   <------Data Transfer----------->
   Firstly the browser sends hello to server to lets connect ,
   then the server sends hello to the the browser ,
   After that the server sends digital certificate to browser,
   then the browser verifies the certificate,
   if certificate is verified then,
   Key exchange occurs then connection is established ,
   and now data transfer can happen smoothly

   What happens if a website's certificate has expired?
   The website is working fine but if we try to access the website , the browser warns us that this is not https secured,
   as it rejects its certificate.

   What are Stack Memory and Heap Memory?
 Stack memory is the memory which is used for execution and storing local variables , such as when a method is called ,
 an instance is created in stack memory and its variables are stored in it.
 Heap memory is the memory where objects of classes are stored.

 Where are Objects stored?
 Objects are stored in heap memory.

 Where are Local Variables stored?
 Local variables are stored in stack memory.

 What is Garbage Collection?
 It is an automatic process where jvm finds objects which are no longer used and no longer reachable  and removes it from the memory .

 What causes Memory Leaks in Java?
 A memory leak happens when an object is no longer needed but still reachable so jvm is not able to remove it cause memory leak.





